<title>CHILE: Endesa reports lower 96 net.</title>
<headline>Endesa reports lower 96 net.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's Empresa Nacional de Electricidad SA (Chile) (Endesa), reported net consolidated earnings of 141.2 billion pesos in 1996, down 12.7 percent from 1995, the company said.</p>
<p>Endesa said the fall in its profits was due to lower income from energy sales in Chile as a result of lower generating prices and higher costs caused by drought.</p>
<p>The company did not give details of its operating earnings, sales earnings or comparative figures.</p>
<p>--Maragret Orgill, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
